//! http-query — the one canonical query-string decoder for constrained
//! Ferrite apps.
//!
//! # Why this package exists
//!
//! `IngressRequest.path` carries `path?query` verbatim, so every app decodes
//! the query itself. applications grew eight hand-rolled decoders that disagree on
//! every edge, and the divergence is a recorded platform gap. Two of the
//! disagreements were shipped defects in a relay application: a browser sent a
//! stream cursor's `:` as `%3A`, the undecoded value failed `Cursor::parse`,
//! and the caller read a failed parse as *no cursor supplied*, so a
//! reconnecting client resumed at the wrong offset with no error anywhere;
//! and `?debug&token=x` returned `None` for `token`, because the pair with no
//! `=` abandoned the whole scan, so a valid caller was refused.
//!
//! Both failures are silently-wrong-answer failures, and both come from a
//! decoder that is partial. This one is total: it cannot fail and it cannot
//! panic, so a hostile target produces a defined answer rather than an error
//! path nobody wrote.
//!
//! It is one module in its own package rather than a module of `agent-ready`
//! because a `ferrite-pkg` mount is all-or-nothing: the three applications
//! with their own MCP faces are the apps whose decoders diverged most,
//! and mounting the whole readiness stack into any of them would put a second
//! MCP face beside `packages/mcp`. `agent-ready` depends on this package, so
//! the readiness consumers keep reaching the decoder at
//! `crate::<mount>::query` and there is still exactly one implementation.
//!
//! # The contract
//!
//! Each edge below is a deliberate decision, and the table is the contract —
//! `parse_query_decodes_every_edge` in this module's tests is the executable
//! copy of it. Change a row only by changing that test first.
//!
//! | Input edge | Decision | Why |
//! | --- | --- | --- |
//! | `+` in a name or a value | becomes a space | A browser submitting a GET form emits `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`, where `+` IS a space. A literal plus must arrive as `%2B`, which every URL encoder produces. |
//! | `%XX`, either hex case | becomes that byte | RFC 3986 §2.1. Rejecting lowercase hex would refuse `URLSearchParams` output. |
//! | `%ZZ`, `%4`, a trailing `%` | passes through verbatim | Totality. A hand-written link carrying a bare `%` must not error, and the platform's own percent-decoder semantics already do this. |
//! | the name as well as the value | decoded identically | `a%2Eb=1` must match a lookup for `a.b`. Decoding one half and not the other is the divergence this module exists to remove. |
//! | a pair with no `=` (`?debug`) | `("debug", "")` | A shipped incident: abandoning the scan hid a token that WAS present. One odd parameter must not break authentication. |
//! | a pair with an empty value (`a=`) | `("a", "")` | Present-and-empty is not absent, and it is deliberately indistinguishable from the row above: no caller has ever needed to tell them apart, and a third state would be a third semantics. |
